    "created_at": "2018-10-04T14:34:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-04T14:34:36Z",
    "body": "> Should TAB keyboard navigation should visit scrollable area?\r\n\r\nI really think so. Otherwise, clipped text in some overflow-divs won't be readable for users who can't, or doesn't want to, use a mouse to click+scroll the area.\r\n\r\nCan we agree to that the current spec holds => scrollers should have tabIndex=0?\r\n\r\nI need to confirm this before I [fix this in Chrome](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/1258331) and submit bugs on Safari and Edge.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
