    "created_at": "2019-09-24T06:56:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-24T06:56:21Z",
    "body": "I think with https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/1ab7c860732d8a1c144ebb86bd08c90f1be7b958 this is as defined as it is going to get. Browsers still want the freedom to choose whether something is focusable, and if so, in what ways, so we're not going to be able to say scrollable areas are always one way or another in the spec. But the spec now has infrastructure for precisely choosing the behavior, and e.g. how this impacts the tabIndex getter (it doesn't).",
